/*
To use this file:

1. Install REST Client extension in VS Code
2. Open this file in VS Code
3. Click "Send Request" above any request
4. View responses in the side panel

OR

1. Copy individual requests to Postman/Thunder Client
2. Replace placeholders (YOUR_PACKAGE_ID_HERE) with actual IDs from your database
3. Test each endpoint

Expected Results:
- All GET requests should return 200 with data
- Valid POST requests should return 201 with success message
- Invalid requests should return 400 with error details
- Non-existent resources should return 404
- Invalid IDs should return 400

Before Testing:
1. Ensure MongoDB is running
2. Ensure server is running on port 5000 (or update URLs)
3. Ensure database has some sample data
4. Update placeholder IDs with actual IDs from your database
*/
